{
  "title": "AGTTM Part 9 - Sample Layouts",
  "abstract": "AGTTM Part 9 is a comprehensive visual reference containing sample Traffic Guidance Scheme layouts for a wide range of traffic management scenarios. It provides standardized diagram templates that can be adapted to specific site conditions.\n\nThe guide contains hundreds of sample layouts organized by work type and road environment. Categories include lane closures on multi-lane roads, single lane closures on two-way roads, shoulder closures, intersection treatments, pedestrian management, and road closures with detours. Each layout includes signage schedules, taper lengths, and spacing requirements.\n\nThese sample layouts form the basis for most pre-approved Traffic Management Plans including MRWA's regional TMPs. Traffic Management Designers use these layouts as templates, adapting them to site-specific conditions. The layouts illustrate the application of requirements from Parts 3, 4, and 5, showing how theoretical requirements translate into practical setups.",
